    <version>0.3.0</version>
    <time>1788018221</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.3.0

requires_dist unchanged. 0.3.0 newly claims /usr/bin/modelscope and
/usr/bin/ms, which python-modelscope 1.39.1 already owns and pulls in via
Requires - a hard file conflict. Both are removed in %install (bare rm,
so the build breaks loudly once upstream resolves script ownership).
133 tests pass.</comment>
    <requestid>1374589</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="3" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>64a4a5a1f00b1228a068feec98eaa914</srcmd5>
    <version>0.3.1</version>
    <time>1788361213</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.3.1

- Upload tunables renamed to canonical MODELSCOPE_UPLOAD_* names that spell out
  their unit; the old names still work but emit a FutureWarning.
- Folder upload caching now defaults to MODELSCOPE_UPLOAD_CACHE_ENABLED instead
  of a hardcoded True, for both the API and the CLI --use-cache flag.
- MCP servers listed via GET /mcp/servers, falling back to the legacy PUT and
  retrying anonymously when a stale or readonly token is rejected.
- Legacy AIGC create_model/create_model_tag take readme_content; create_model_tag
  reconciles a timed-out tag against the remote revision list.

Built locally on aarch64 and green on OBS x86_64 at srcmd5
64a4a5a1f00b1228a068feec98eaa914: 177 tests pass per Python flavour,
rpmlint 0 errors / 0 badness.</comment>
    <requestid>1375188</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
